1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,721
As a teenager, he washed dishes and bussed

2
00:00:02,721 --> 00:00:04,626
tables at a Denny's restaurant.

3
00:00:05,276 --> 00:00:07,788
Decades later, the company he co-founded

4
00:00:07,788 --> 00:00:10,184
at a Denny's booth became the first in

5
00:00:10,184 --> 00:00:12,346
history to be worth five trillion

6
00:00:12,346 --> 00:00:12,989
dollars

7
00:00:13,638 --> 00:00:16,444
— more than the entire economy of almost

8
00:00:16,444 --> 00:00:18,140
every country on Earth.

9
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:20,633
His name is Jensen Huang.

10
00:00:20,633 --> 00:00:23,152
His company, NVIDIA, makes the chips

11
00:00:23,152 --> 00:00:25,855
that power most of the world's artificial

12
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:26,838
intelligence.

13
00:00:27,488 --> 00:00:29,792
And this week, according to multiple

14
00:00:29,792 --> 00:00:32,155
reports, his own board was discussing

15
00:00:32,155 --> 00:00:33,631
whether to remove him.

16
00:00:34,281 --> 00:00:36,583
This is the story of how one company —

17
00:00:36,583 --> 00:00:38,660
and, for a while, one man — became

18
00:00:38,660 --> 00:00:40,513
something engineers fear most:

19
00:00:41,163 --> 00:00:43,055
a single point of failure.

20
00:00:43,055 --> 00:00:45,192
For an entire technological age.

21
00:00:45,842 --> 00:00:47,733
Quick favor before we start:

22
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:50,355
if you like stories about the people and

23
00:00:50,355 --> 00:00:52,794
